\title{Spin-representation roadmap}

\p{This appendix follows the mathematical dependencies organized by the
\href{https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCetiRoadmap/tree/main/TauCetiRoadmap/RepresentationTheory/SpinRepresentations}{spin-representation roadmap}
and the
\href{https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCetiRoadmap/tree/main/TauCetiRoadmap/OrthogonalSpinGroups}{orthogonal Spin-groups roadmap}
of \href{https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti}{Tau Ceti}. The first
organizes the filtered Clifford algebra, bivectors, spinor modules, and real
classification. The second organizes reflections, the Pin and Spin covers,
Clifford norms, and the orthogonal action. These roadmaps guide the scope and
dependencies below; formalization links refer to specific landed declarations.}

\p{The filtered Clifford algebra first exposes its exterior shadow.
Reflections then lead to the global Pin and Spin extensions, while bivectors
provide the algebraic infinitesimal orthogonal action. A polar-dual basis turns
that action into a coordinate lift, and the Killing pairing gives the adjoint
case. The Lie functor records the separate differential bridge from smooth
group homomorphisms. A polarization joins the algebraic group and Lie
constructions in the exterior spinor model. The real-signature recurrence and
classification form a parallel algebraic branch and do not depend on the
spinor-module or double-cover join.}

